# Cloudflare Pages routing.
#
# Order matters. Pages serves a matching static file first, then walks these
# rules top to bottom.
#
# Rule 1 exists because of a real incident on a sibling project: Pages served
# index.html (200, text/html) for a missing /assets/* path, and the
# `immutable, max-age=31536000` header in public/_headers then stamped that
# HTML body into the zone edge cache for a year at an asset URL. Pages' own
# deploy purge does not touch the zone cache, and the wrangler OAuth on this
# machine has zone:read only, so it could not be purged.
#
# A missing hashed asset must fail loudly, not be cached as HTML forever.
/assets/*   /asset-not-found.html   404

# Rule 2 is the SPA fallback that react-router needs. It was previously
# implicit — Pages falls back to index.html when a project has no 404.html.
# Stating it explicitly means rule 1 above cannot accidentally turn the whole
# site into hard 404s, and the behaviour no longer depends on the absence of
# a file.
/*          /index.html             200
